      title: "SEO Content That Ranks—and Converts Visitors into Clients",
      excerpt:
        "Keyword research is only half the battle. Here is how we pair search intent with compelling narrative structure and high-converting calls to action.",
      content: `
      <h2>The Problem With Traffic That Doesn't Convert</h2>
      <p>Ranking #1 on Google for high-volume keywords feels great, but if those visitors bounce within 15 seconds without taking action, your marketing ROI is zero.</p>

      <h3>1. Aligning With Searcher Intent</h3>
      <p>Search engines now prioritize topical authority and user satisfaction above keyword density. We break down content strategy into four clear intent buckets:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Informational:</strong> Comprehensive guides addressing immediate pain points.</li>
        <li><strong>Commercial Investigation:</strong> Comparison articles, benchmarks, and honest reviews.</li>
        <li><strong>Transactional:</strong> High-converting landing pages tailored for ready-to-buy decision-makers.</li>
        <li><strong>Navigational:</strong> Clean brand pathways and documentation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Designing for Skimmability</h3>
      <p>Modern readers scan. Using crisp subheadings, bullet points, callout boxes, and contextual visual diagrams keeps readers engaged from the opening hook all the way down to the final conversion form.</p>
    `,
